{"family": "memfof", "task": "flow", "name": "MEMFOF", "plain": "MEMFOF (MSU Graphics & Media Lab, ICCV 2025): memory-efficient multi-frame optical flow, a RAFT-style network that also looks at the previous frame and runs at full HD. BSD-3-Clause code and weights; some training sets are research-only.", "summary": "MEMFOF (Bargatin et al. 2025): memory-efficient multi-frame optical flow. A RAFT-style network at 1/16 resolution on three frames: a ResNet34 context encoder on all three, a GMA attention over the context, 1024-channel features with an all-pairs correlation pyramid toward the previous and the next frame, a ConvNeXt update block and convex 16x upsampling; it predicts the backward and the forward flow of the middle frame at once. The authors' released weights; the network is ported from msu-video-group/memfof. A pair (image1, image2) runs as upstream's first frame of a clip, the frames (image1, image1, image2), and returns its forward flow. Paper (three frames per prediction, the fine-tuned checkpoints): Spring test 1px 3.289 %, Sintel test EPE 0.963 (clean), KITTI 2015 test Fl-all 2.94 %.", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/msu-video-group/memfof", "upstream_commit": "a51de9fc59c6fe20ba08e079372c7b583d58a712", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "MEMFOF: High-Resolution Training for Memory-Efficient Multi-Frame Optical Flow Estimation", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.23151", "date": "2025-06-29", "venue": "ICCV 2025", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["raft_flow", "flow_upsample"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "iters", "default": 8, "bounds": ">= 1", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "flow", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE", "LICENSE-torchvision"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["Pairs only: the multi-frame input (a previous frame and the feature cache of upstream's video demo) is not exposed; each pair runs as the first frame of a clip.", "Full-frame 1080x1920 runs out of memory on the RTX 5060 Ti 16 GB in the upstream original and in portable; only kernels fit (7.2 GB).", "At fixed 384 x 1248, the TensorRT ResNet encoders took about 1.33 s versus 1.53 s for paired portable FP32 on the KITTI and Sintel checkpoints. The rest of the flow pipeline ran in PyTorch. The first ten KITTI pairs had at most 0.00002 px of endpoint-error change for either checkpoint."], "task_io": "Input: two RGB images (consecutive frames). Output: per-pixel motion from the first to the second (dx, dy in pixels).", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "memfof", "released": "0.3.0", "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "memfof@1", "name": "memfof", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "BSD-3-Clause", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "BSD-3-Clause", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://huggingface.co/egorchistov/optical-flow-MEMFOF-Tartan-T-TSKH/blob/6c6c9aa3ad64f93aee8efbc2f7a6e4535814ee96/README.md", "training_data": [{"id": "tartanair", "name": "TartanAir", "licence": "CC-BY-4.0", "commercial": "yes", "url": "https://theairlab.org/tartanair-dataset/"}, {"id": "sceneflow", "name": "Freiburg SceneFlow (FlyingThings3D, Driving, Monkaa)", "licence": "LicenseRef-research-only", "commercial": "no", "url": "https://lmb.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/resources/datasets/SceneFlowDatasets.en.html"}, {"id": "sintel-flow", "name": "MPI Sintel optical flow", "licence": "LicenseRef-noncommercial", "commercial": "no", "url": "https://sintel.is.tue.mpg.de/license"}, {"id": "kitti", "name": "KITTI stereo / optical flow 2012 / 2015", "licence": "CC-BY-NC-SA-3.0", "commercial": "no", "url": "https://www.cvlibs.net/datasets/kitti/"}, {"id": "hd1k", "name": "HCI HD1K optical flow benchmark", "licence": "not stated"